# goal-nudge-backoff-epoch-rearm: R23. A saturated goal (consecutiveNoResolveNudges=MAX,
# nudgeSeq=3, backoffTicksRemaining=2) whose legacy nudges (seq 1..3) predate the CURRENT
# all-idle epoch anchor must re-arm on the first eligible tick: the cap branch detects the
# anchor postdates the last emission (prior epoch's nudges are idle_epoch_advanced-invalidated
# and no turn_end resolve could fire while starved), resets the counter ONCE per anchor, and
# emits the fresh seq=4 nudge. Pre-R23 the pump looped backoff.skip → backoff_just_exhausted →
# max_nudges re-arm forever (zero goal.idle_nudge, zero pi.sendMessage).
#
# Pattern 2 (seeded world + single-actor script) per .agents/skills/mock-llm-scenarios/SKILL.md:
# launch.sh seeds goal-r23-fixture (user-origin, saturated), 3 legacy mailbox_delivered nudges
# (msg-r23-rearm-1/2/3, createdAt BEFORE the anchor), allIdleSinceAt = seed-time (anchor strictly
# after every legacy createdAt), idle worker, PI_SWARM_GOAL_NUDGE_IDLE_INTERVAL_MS=1000 so the
# first pump tick is eligible. Evidence cites (independent):
#   C1 durable append: goal:goal-r23-fixture:nudge:idle-streak:4 message + goal.idle_nudge trace
#      (seq:4, consecutiveCount:1) + goal.nudge.saturation_reset_on_epoch trace;
#   C3 real send: mailbox.root_pump count>=1 (pi.sendMessage at the pump boundary);
#   C4 no starvation: notification.stale.suppressed ABSENT for goal keys;
#   C5 LLM consumption: this script's swarm_check_mailbox + swarm_ack_message tool calls run in
#      the root turn AFTER the surfaced nudge (provider transcript records them).
